{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis","id":1347420,"title":"Fake/Overstated/Misunderstood Deities and Recent Apotheosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-10T01:01:20-08:00","id":1347420,"title":"Fake/Overstated/Misunderstood Deities and Recent Apotheosis","content":"What do you guys think about the idea of gods who either didn't really exist historically or whose importance was greatly overstated in pop-culture being Scions of their respective pantheons who ascended after their pantheon's heyday? For instance, &quot;Radegast&quot; being a modern Bogovi Scion who ascended to godhood relatively recently, or Brighid being an incarnate Scion of the exceedingly minor wife of Bres who greatly outdid all of her previous incarnates in importance and prevalence? Perhaps Ah Puch was a Scion of Yum Cimil who recently ascended and now serves as a rival of his patron/father, and Mikaboshi is, as discussed on the thread about him, a modern Kami Titan Scion? And so on and so forth. Just a thought. Santoshi, the Deva of satisfaction, who was made up for a movie but assumed to be &quot;real&quot; and basically became so because of it could be an interesting case study of this happening. (Thanks to Samudra for pointing her out to me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T01:35:15-08:00","id":1347424,"title":"","content":"I rather like the idea. Pop culture especially is filled with these sort of weird, invented (via misunderstanding or other causes) additions to various mythologies, and IMO at least this sort of thing seems to fit the game's cosmology. It also gives a GM the opportunity to surprise players with an antagonist or other important NPC they weren't expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T03:25:43-08:00","id":1347434,"title":"","content":"Well, our characters are basically that, new gods to the pantheon that become somehow important, so we must be really open minded about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T10:23:45-08:00","id":1347709,"title":"","content":"The Daijingu Shrine in Hawai'i has George Washington as a kami under Amaterasu Omikami. Om Banna in Rajasthan is a deity believed to protect people from motorcycle accidents. And other cases around the world with active storytelling show that religious figures keep getting added to their pantheons. Using modern folk examples for Scion can be a good place to draw inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T15:24:28-08:00","id":1347777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis#post1347420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think about the idea of gods who either didn't really exist historically or whose importance was greatly overstated in pop-culture being Scions of their respective pantheons who ascended after their pantheon's heyday? For instance, &amp;quot;Radegast&amp;quot; being a modern Bogovi Scion who ascended to godhood relatively recently, or Brighid being an incarnate Scion of the exceedingly minor wife of Bres who greatly outdid all of her previous incarnates in importance and prevalence? Perhaps Ah Puch was a Scion of Yum Cimil who recently ascended and now serves as a rival of his patron/father, and Mikaboshi is, as discussed on the thread about him, a modern Kami Titan Scion? And so on and so forth. Just a thought. Santoshi, the Deva of satisfaction, who was made up for a movie but assumed to be &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; and basically became so because of it could be an interesting case study of this happening. (Thanks to Samudra for pointing her out to me.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I\u2019ve considered Bridig the fire-goddess being a later apotheosis as well!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:51:30-08:00","id":1347794,"title":"","content":"You can also have famous figures who died as Heroes or Demigods.<br /> And either use them as reincarnations as new mortals or have their ghosts as Guides.<br /> <br /> Im also fiddling with using a concept derived from Mantles that i call Tatters or Rags. Not quite mantles that nevertheless managed to gain some manner of ... fateful momentum.<br /> <br /> Anyway these figures dont have to be gods to be used in a game i think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T06:16:16-08:00","id":1347877,"title":"","content":"Just as an addendum, Pantheons don't just always include new <i>Gods</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/736x/56/79/57/5679572b7c6cfb04e6ed70317826dfe2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> (For clarity, Thanos isn't actually an official Asura, but idols like these were popular after Infinity War in India, and is a great example of how much religions aren't static things but always evolving)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 11-12-2019, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:17:17-08:00","id":1348043,"title":"","content":"That's absolutely fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T16:56:46-08:00","id":1348064,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and this isn't even getting to people who might be worshiped by different cultures as members of a pantheon (Japanese Shrines in Hawaii include figures like King Kamehameha the Great and George Washington, when they obviously aren't considered kami by the Japanese who live on Japan). Religions aren't static in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23543-penguinbowler","name":"Penguinbowler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T20:07:03-08:00","id":1348987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1347777#post1347777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I\u2019ve considered Bridig the fire-goddess being a later apotheosis as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>The only role in actual recorded Irish myth that Bridig has is as the inventor of keening. Yet they never seem to give Bridig the Death purview.<br /> <br /> Oh I get my facts from the book &quot;Ireland's Immortals.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-16T20:22:19-08:00","id":1348992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1348987#post1348987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only role in actual recorded Irish myth that Bridig has is as the inventor of keening. Yet they never seem to give Bridig the Death purview.<br /> <br /> Oh I get my facts from the book &quot;Ireland's Immortals.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>specifically, IIRC, the fire goddess is based on Medieval English claims about the pagan Irish to justify Christianizing invasion forces (they were already Christian of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T19:30:21-08:00","id":1349245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1347877#post1347877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as an addendum, Pantheons don't just always include new <i>Gods</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (For clarity, Thanos isn't actually an official Asura, but idols like these were popular after Infinity War in India, and is a great example of how much religions aren't static things but always evolving)</div> </div> </div> </div>IS that Hercules in there as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T13:36:27-08:00","id":1349432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1349245#post1349245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IS that Hercules in there as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is Mahishasura, the Buffalo Titan, the Goddess Durga's most famous opponent in myth. The Lion he's wrestling with (which I assume was part of the confusion?) is not the Nemean Lion but Durga's Vahana, the sacred beast she rides into battle and her constant companion. The Lion aids Durga in battle and once famously slaughtered 60,000 Titans in a few moments:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6.15 Then the lion, the Dev\u012b\u2019s mount, angrily shook its mane. Emitting a terrifying roar, it fell upon the demon army. <br /> <br /> 6.16 With blows of its paws, it slew some daityas and crushed others in its jaws. And it trampled other great asuras under its hind legs. <br /> <br /> 6.17 With its claws, the lion tore into the entrails of some and beheaded others with the stroke of a paw. <br /> <br /> 6.18 It tore the arms and heads off others still, and tossing its mane, it lapped up the blood from the bellies of others. <br /> <br /> 6.19 In an instant that noble, infuriated lion which bore the Dev\u012b wreaked destruction on all that army. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T19:20:24-08:00","id":1349489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1349432#post1349432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that is Mahishasura, the Buffalo Titan, the Goddess Durga's most famous opponent in myth. The Lion he's wrestling with (which I assume was part of the confusion?) is not the Nemean Lion but Durga's Vahana, the sacred beast she rides into battle and her constant companion. The Lion aids Durga in battle and once famously slaughtered 60,000 Titans in a few moments:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah just curious since he looks ALOT like Marvel Hercules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T19:27:08-08:00","id":1349491,"title":"","content":"It amazes me just how devastatingly powerful the Devas truly are. That's quite badass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T22:50:23-08:00","id":1349502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1347420-fake-overstated-misunderstood-deities-and-recent-apotheosis?p=1349491#post1349491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It amazes me just how devastatingly powerful the Devas truly are. That's quite badass.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes, incidentally, right after Durga shushes a guy to death... as in some Titan threatens to drag her kicking and screaming to his King to force her to marry him, and she goes 'harumph' at him and he <i>disintegrates</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6.7 \u201cCommanded thus by \u015aumbha, the daitya Dh\u016bmralocana quickly set off, accompanied by sixty thousand asuras. <br /> <br /> 6.8 And when he saw the Dev\u012b stationed on the snowy mountain, he thundered, \u2018Come to the presence of \u015aumbha and Ni\u015bumbha. <br /> <br /> 6.9 And if her highness will not come in gladness to my master now, then I will take her by force, dragging her by the hair, kicking and screaming.\u2019 <br /> <br /> 6.10 The Dev\u012b said: <br /> <br /> 6.11 \u2018You who are sent by the lord of the daityas are mighty yourself and accompanied by your army. If you take me by force, what can I do to you?\u2019\u201d <br /> <br /> 6.12 The seer said: <br /> <br /> 6.13 \u201cThus addressed, the asura Dh\u016bmralocana rushed at her. Thereupon, with a contemptuous outcry, Ambik\u0101 reduced him to ashes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T03:12:08-08:00","id":1349537,"title":"","content":"Good for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T15:18:08-08:00","id":1349700,"title":"","content":"I love Durga, and wish there were epic globally released movies about her. That or totally awesome anime series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}